gaps.proposedFix:
Define `as` per slice, symmetric with `value`; a slice carrying BOTH means assert-and-capture:
{ "bits": [ {"n":2,"as":"li"}, {"n":3,"value":"4","as":"vn"}, {"n":3,"as":"mode"} ] }
Slices bind capture.li / capture.vn / capture.mode as Int; sum(n) must be a multiple of 8 (validate-time check, already implied). Encode ignores `as`, decode ignores `value` except as an equality assertion.

Add a `negotiates` block to a message, evaluated on successful decode:
  "ntpServerResponse": {
    "negotiates": {
      "vn":       { "from":"capture.vn",       "rule":"min",
                    "into":"store.vn",         "reject":"capture.vn < 3" },
      "pollLog2": { "from":"capture.pollLog2", "rule":"max",
                    "clamp":["inputs.minPollLog2","inputs.maxPollLog2"],
                    "into":"store.pollLog2" } } }
`rule` in { min, max, intersect, replace }; `into` is a store/session path that subsequent encodes read. Generalises directly to MQTT SUBACK granted-QoS, TLS cipher selection, and CoAP Block2 size negotiation.
